<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Theodore II Muzaka</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1389">1389</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Theodore II Muzaka (died 1389) was an Albanian lord of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muzaka-family">Muzaka family</a> who held <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berat">Berat</a> and the surrounding region of central Albania in the late 14th century. According to tradition he died fighting the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> in the Serbian-led coalition at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-kosovo">Battle of Kosovo</a> in 1389. His family remained one of the leading Albanian noble houses until the Ottoman conquest.</p></div>
